IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `nsw-nouns`

-- Interpretation Act 1987 (New South Wales), Part 2 Words and expressions: sections 20 to 21D.
-- References to statutory rules, Colony, offences, de facto partners and health practitioners.
-- Facts the Act borrows from other instruments (the Relationships Register Act 2010, the Surrogacy Act 2010,
-- the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law (NSW)) are plain inputs.

§ `Part 2 Words and expressions (continued)`

§§ `20 References to statutory rules etc`

-- The words section 20 defines.
DECLARE StatutoryWord IS ONE OF
    TheWordByLaw
    TheWordOrdinance
    TheWordPrescribed
    TheWordRegulation
    TheWordRule
    AnotherStatutoryWord

-- src:157 | 20 References to statutory rules etc
-- src:158 | In any Act—
-- src:159 | by-law means a by-law made under the Act in which that word occurs.
-- src:160 | ordinance means an ordinance made under the Act in which that word occurs.
-- src:161 | prescribed means prescribed by, or by a statutory rule made under, the Act in which that word occurs.
-- src:162 | regulation means a regulation made under the Act in which that word occurs.
-- src:163 | rule means a rule made under the Act in which that word occurs.
@ref s 20 (src:157-163)
GIVEN word IS A StatutoryWord
      `it is made under the Act in which the word occurs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is prescribed by the Act in which the word occurs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 20 the thing is within the meaning of the word in an Act` MEANS
    CONSIDER word
    WHEN TheWordByLaw THEN JUST `it is made under the Act in which the word occurs`
    WHEN TheWordOrdinance THEN JUST `it is made under the Act in which the word occurs`
    WHEN TheWordPrescribed THEN JUST (`it is prescribed by the Act in which the word occurs` OR `it is made under the Act in which the word occurs`)
    WHEN TheWordRegulation THEN JUST `it is made under the Act in which the word occurs`
    WHEN TheWordRule THEN JUST `it is made under the Act in which the word occurs`
    WHEN AnotherStatutoryWord THEN NOTHING

§§ `21 References to Colony and punishments for offences`

-- The two expressions section 21(2) defines.
DECLARE ColonyExpression IS ONE OF
    ColonyInRelationToAPartOfAustralia
    TheColony
    AnotherExpressionNotInSection21

-- src:167 | (2) In any Act passed before the commencement of this Act, and in any instrument made under such an Act—
-- src:168 | Colony, in relation to any part of Australia, means the State or Territory that corresponds to that part of Australia.
@ref s 21(2) Colony (src:167-168)
GIVEN `the Act was passed before the commencement of this Act, or the instrument is made under such an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 21(2) the meaning of Colony in relation to any part of Australia` MEANS
    IF `the Act was passed before the commencement of this Act, or the instrument is made under such an Act`
    THEN JUST "the State or Territory that corresponds to that part of Australia"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:167 | (2) In any Act passed before the commencement of this Act, and in any instrument made under such an Act—
-- src:168 | Colony, in relation to any part of Australia, means the State or Territory that corresponds to that part of Australia.
-- src:169 | the Colony means the State of New South Wales.
@ref s 21(2) the Colony (src:167-169)
GIVEN `the Act was passed before the commencement of this Act, or the instrument is made under such an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 21(2) the meaning of the Colony` MEANS
    IF `the Act was passed before the commencement of this Act, or the instrument is made under such an Act`
    THEN JUST "the State of New South Wales"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The offences section 21(3) speaks of.
DECLARE OffenceForSection21 IS ONE OF
    ACommonLawOffence
    AnOffencePunishableByImprisonmentForLife
    AnotherOffence

-- src:171 | (a) a reference to an offence that is punishable by imprisonment for a specified term or more includes a reference to a common law offence, and
@ref s 21(3)(a) (src:171)
GIVEN offence IS A OffenceForSection21
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21(3)(a) a reference to an offence punishable by imprisonment for a specified term or more includes a reference to it` MEANS
    CONSIDER offence
    WHEN ACommonLawOffence THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN AnOffencePunishableByImprisonmentForLife THEN NOTHING
    WHEN AnotherOffence THEN NOTHING

-- src:172 | (b) a reference to an offence that is punishable by imprisonment for a specified term or more includes a reference to an offence punishable by imprisonment for life.
@ref s 21(3)(b) (src:172)
GIVEN offence IS A OffenceForSection21
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21(3)(b) a reference to an offence punishable by imprisonment for a specified term or more includes a reference to it` MEANS
    CONSIDER offence
    WHEN AnOffencePunishableByImprisonmentForLife THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN ACommonLawOffence THEN NOTHING
    WHEN AnotherOffence THEN NOTHING

§§ `21C References to de facto partners and de facto relationships`

-- src:177 | (1) Meaning of "de facto partner" For the purposes of any Act or instrument, a person is the de facto partner of another person (whether of the same sex or a different sex) if—
-- src:178 | (a) the person is in a registered relationship or interstate registered relationship with the other person within the meaning of the Relationships Register Act 2010, or
-- src:179 | (b) the person is in a de facto relationship with the other person.
@ref s 21C(1) (src:177-179)
GIVEN `the person is in a registered relationship or interstate registered relationship with the other person within the meaning of the Relationships Register Act 2010` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is in a de facto relationship with the other person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21C(1) the person is the de facto partner of the other person` MEANS
    `the person is in a registered relationship or interstate registered relationship with the other person within the meaning of the Relationships Register Act 2010`
    OR `the person is in a de facto relationship with the other person`

-- src:180 | (2) Meaning of "de facto relationship" For the purposes of any Act or instrument, a person is in a de facto relationship with another person if—
-- src:181 | (a) they have a relationship as a couple living together, and
-- src:182 | (b) they are not married to one another or related by family.
@ref s 21C(2) (src:180-182)
GIVEN `they have a relationship as a couple living together` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are married to one another or related by family` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21C(2) the person is in a de facto relationship with the other person` MEANS
    `they have a relationship as a couple living together` AND (NOT `they are married to one another or related by family`)

-- src:183 | A de facto relationship can exist even if one of the persons is legally married to someone else or in a registered relationship or interstate registered relationship with someone else.
@ref s 21C(2) closing sentence (src:183)
GIVEN `one of the persons is legally married to someone else` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one of the persons is in a registered relationship or interstate registered relationship with someone else` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21C(2) the marriage or registered relationship with someone else prevents a de facto relationship from existing` MEANS
    IF `one of the persons is legally married to someone else` OR `one of the persons is in a registered relationship or interstate registered relationship with someone else`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The matters section 21C(3) lists.
DECLARE RelationshipMatter IS ONE OF
    TheDurationOfTheRelationship
    TheNatureAndExtentOfTheirCommonResidence
    WhetherASexualRelationshipExists
    TheDegreeOfFinancialDependenceOrInterdependence
    TheOwnershipUseAndAcquisitionOfProperty
    TheDegreeOfMutualCommitmentToASharedLife
    TheCareAndSupportOfChildren
    ThePerformanceOfHouseholdDuties
    TheReputationAndPublicAspectsOfTheRelationship
    AnotherCircumstanceOfTheRelationship

-- src:184 | (3) Determination of "relationship as a couple" In determining whether 2 persons have a relationship as a couple for the purposes of subsection (2), all the circumstances of the relationship are to be taken into account, including any of the following matters that are relevant in a particular case—
-- src:185 | (a) the duration of the relationship,
-- src:186 | (b) the nature and extent of their common residence,
-- src:187 | (c) whether a sexual relationship exists,
-- src:188 | (d) the degree of financial dependence or interdependence, and any arrangements for financial support, between them,
-- src:189 | (e) the ownership, use and acquisition of property,
-- src:190 | (f) the degree of mutual commitment to a shared life,
-- src:191 | (g) the care and support of children,
-- src:192 | (h) the performance of household duties,
-- src:193 | (i) the reputation and public aspects of the relationship.
@ref s 21C(3) (src:184-193)
GIVEN matter IS A RelationshipMatter
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21C(3) the matter is taken into account in determining whether they have a relationship as a couple` MEANS
    TRUE

-- src:194 | No particular finding in relation to any of those matters is necessary in determining whether 2 persons have a relationship as a couple.
@ref s 21C(3) closing sentence (src:194)
GIVEN matter IS A RelationshipMatter
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21C(3) a particular finding on the matter is necessary` MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN AnotherCircumstanceOfTheRelationship THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:195 | (4) Meaning of "related by family" For the purposes of subsection (2), 2 persons are related by family if—
-- src:196 | (a) one is the child (including an adopted child) of the other, or
-- src:197 | (b) one is another descendant of the other (even if the relationship between them is traced through an adoptive parent), or
-- src:198 | (c) they have a parent in common (including an adoptive parent of either or both of them).
@ref s 21C(4) (src:195-198)
GIVEN `one is the child (including an adopted child) of the other` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one is another descendant of the other (even if traced through an adoptive parent)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they have a parent in common (including an adoptive parent of either or both of them)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21C(4) the two persons are related by family` MEANS
        `one is the child (including an adopted child) of the other`
     OR `one is another descendant of the other (even if traced through an adoptive parent)`
     OR `they have a parent in common (including an adoptive parent of either or both of them)`

-- src:199 | (5) Subsection (4) applies—
-- src:200 | (a) even if an adoption has been declared void or is of no effect, and
-- src:201 | (b) to adoptions under the law of any place (whether in or out of Australia) relating to the adoption of children.
@ref s 21C(5) (src:199-201)
GIVEN `there was an adoption` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the adoption has been declared void or is of no effect` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the adoption was under the law of a place (in or out of Australia) relating to the adoption of children` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21C(5) subsection (4) applies to the adoption` MEANS
    IF `there was an adoption` AND `the adoption was under the law of a place (in or out of Australia) relating to the adoption of children`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:202 | (6) Subsection (4) applies in relation to a child whose parentage is transferred as a result of a parentage order, or an Interstate parentage order, within the meaning of the Surrogacy Act 2010 in the same way as it applies in relation to an adopted child, even if the parentage order is discharged or otherwise ceases to have effect. For that purpose, a reference in that subsection to an adoptive parent is to be read as a reference to a person to whom the parentage of a child is transferred under such a parentage order.
@ref s 21C(6) (src:202)
GIVEN `the parentage of the child is transferred by a parentage order or Interstate parentage order within the meaning of the Surrogacy Act 2010` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order is discharged or otherwise ceases to have effect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21C(6) subsection (4) applies to the child in the same way as to an adopted child` MEANS
    IF `the parentage of the child is transferred by a parentage order or Interstate parentage order within the meaning of the Surrogacy Act 2010`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `21D References to health practitioners`

-- src:205 | (1) In any Act or instrument, a reference to a named class of health practitioner in a health profession within the meaning of the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law (NSW) means a person who, under that Law, is registered (other than as a student) and is authorised to use that name.
@ref s 21D(1) (src:205)
GIVEN `the person is registered under the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law (NSW) in that class` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the registration is as a student` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is authorised to use that name under that Law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21D(1) the reference to a named class of health practitioner means the person` MEANS
        `the person is registered under the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law (NSW) in that class`
    AND (NOT `the registration is as a student`)
    AND `the person is authorised to use that name under that Law`

-- src:206 | (2) However, if the reference is to a registered nurse this is taken not to include a reference to a person who is registered under that Law as an enrolled nurse.
@ref s 21D(2) (src:206)
GIVEN `the reference is to a registered nurse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is registered under that Law as an enrolled nurse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21D(2) the reference to a registered nurse includes the person` MEANS
    IF `the reference is to a registered nurse` AND `the person is registered under that Law as an enrolled nurse`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Tests: sections 20 to 21D`

-- s 20: by-law, ordinance, regulation and rule mean one made under the Act in which the word occurs; prescribed also covers the Act itself
#ASSERT `s 20 the thing is within the meaning of the word in an Act` TheWordByLaw TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 20 the thing is within the meaning of the word in an Act` TheWordByLaw FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 20 the thing is within the meaning of the word in an Act` TheWordOrdinance TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 20 the thing is within the meaning of the word in an Act` TheWordOrdinance FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 20 the thing is within the meaning of the word in an Act` TheWordRegulation TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 20 the thing is within the meaning of the word in an Act` TheWordRegulation FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 20 the thing is within the meaning of the word in an Act` TheWordRule TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 20 the thing is within the meaning of the word in an Act` TheWordRule FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 20 the thing is within the meaning of the word in an Act` TheWordPrescribed FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 20 the thing is within the meaning of the word in an Act` TheWordPrescribed TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 20 the thing is within the meaning of the word in an Act` TheWordPrescribed FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 20 the thing is within the meaning of the word in an Act` AnotherStatutoryWord TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 21(2)
#ASSERT `s 21(2) the meaning of Colony in relation to any part of Australia` TRUE EQUALS JUST "the State or Territory that corresponds to that part of Australia"
#ASSERT `s 21(2) the meaning of Colony in relation to any part of Australia` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 21(2) the meaning of the Colony` TRUE EQUALS JUST "the State of New South Wales"
#ASSERT `s 21(2) the meaning of the Colony` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 21(3)
#ASSERT `s 21(3)(a) a reference to an offence punishable by imprisonment for a specified term or more includes a reference to it` ACommonLawOffence EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 21(3)(a) a reference to an offence punishable by imprisonment for a specified term or more includes a reference to it` AnotherOffence EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 21(3)(b) a reference to an offence punishable by imprisonment for a specified term or more includes a reference to it` AnOffencePunishableByImprisonmentForLife EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 21(3)(b) a reference to an offence punishable by imprisonment for a specified term or more includes a reference to it` AnotherOffence EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 21C(1)
#ASSERT `s 21C(1) the person is the de facto partner of the other person` TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 21C(1) the person is the de facto partner of the other person` FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 21C(1) the person is the de facto partner of the other person` FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- s 21C(2)
#ASSERT `s 21C(2) the person is in a de facto relationship with the other person` TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 21C(2) the person is in a de facto relationship with the other person` TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 21C(2) the person is in a de facto relationship with the other person` FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 21C(2) the marriage or registered relationship with someone else prevents a de facto relationship from existing` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 21C(2) the marriage or registered relationship with someone else prevents a de facto relationship from existing` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 21C(2) the marriage or registered relationship with someone else prevents a de facto relationship from existing` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 21C(3): each of the nine matters is taken into account and none needs a particular finding; any other circumstance is taken into account and the Act does not say whether a finding on it is necessary
#ASSERT `s 21C(3) the matter is taken into account in determining whether they have a relationship as a couple` TheDurationOfTheRelationship EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 21C(3) the matter is taken into account in determining whether they have a relationship as a couple` TheReputationAndPublicAspectsOfTheRelationship EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 21C(3) the matter is taken into account in determining whether they have a relationship as a couple` AnotherCircumstanceOfTheRelationship EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 21C(3) a particular finding on the matter is necessary` WhetherASexualRelationshipExists EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 21C(3) a particular finding on the matter is necessary` TheCareAndSupportOfChildren EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 21C(3) a particular finding on the matter is necessary` AnotherCircumstanceOfTheRelationship EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 21C(4): any one of the three ties
#ASSERT `s 21C(4) the two persons are related by family` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 21C(4) the two persons are related by family` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 21C(4) the two persons are related by family` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 21C(4) the two persons are related by family` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- s 21C(5): an adoption counts whether or not it has been declared void; one not under such a law is not covered
#ASSERT `s 21C(5) subsection (4) applies to the adoption` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 21C(5) subsection (4) applies to the adoption` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 21C(5) subsection (4) applies to the adoption` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 21C(5) subsection (4) applies to the adoption` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 21C(6): a parentage order, even if later discharged
#ASSERT `s 21C(6) subsection (4) applies to the child in the same way as to an adopted child` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 21C(6) subsection (4) applies to the child in the same way as to an adopted child` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 21C(6) subsection (4) applies to the child in the same way as to an adopted child` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 21D
#ASSERT `s 21D(1) the reference to a named class of health practitioner means the person` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 21D(1) the reference to a named class of health practitioner means the person` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 21D(1) the reference to a named class of health practitioner means the person` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 21D(1) the reference to a named class of health practitioner means the person` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 21D(2) the reference to a registered nurse includes the person` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 21D(2) the reference to a registered nurse includes the person` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 21D(2) the reference to a registered nurse includes the person` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
